    "notes": "Laterally compressed caridean shrimp. Cephalothorax about a quarter of body length (16 mm of 60 mm) and about 0.7 as deep as long, deeper than wide, blunt anterior margin with an upturned rostrum reaching a further 8.5 mm; abdomen of six telescoping pleomeres (the sixth elongated) about half the body length, with a dorsal hump at pleomere 2-3 descending to a flat telson with two pairs of uropod blades. Stalked eyes below the rostrum, forked antennules, antennal scales, and long white second antennae. Five pairs of slender pereiopods, pairs 1 and 2 chelate; third maxillipeds project forward under the mouth; five pairs of pleopod paddles under pleomeres 1 to 5.",
